:"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"blind_id\":\"ST033\",\"coverage\":[{\"point\":1,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"States the 75-day Rule 485(a)(2) period for a new-series amendment and contrasts it with 60 days for other amendments. Notes SEC acceleration and registrant delay, says the clock is not a launch guarantee, and correctly separates new-trust registration (N-8A/N-1A under §8(a), 20 days nominal, Rule 473 delaying amendment, 'no 485 timeline applies').\"},{\"point\":2,\"credit\":0,\"reason\":\"Optional point: does not explicitly say shares cannot be sold before effectiveness and gives no filed example. Optional omissions do not reduce the grade.\"},{\"point\":3,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"Says the filing clock is not an overall launch deadline and lists added steps: staff comments, 485(b) final filing and delays, board approvals, Form 8-A, exchange listing under generic standards or 19b-4, CUSIP, seed capital, APs, custody, index licensing and service contracts. The 95-day limit is optional and its omission is not penalized.\"}],\"central_error\":null,\"local_error\":null,\"grade\":\"correct\",\"rationale\":\"Both required points are fully covered. There is no central error: 75 days is tied only to the new-series amendment, is expressly not a launch guarantee, and is excluded from initial trust registration. Ancillary statements (60-day 485(a)(1), 485(b)(1)(iii) delay, 6c-11 generic listing, N-8A/§8(a) 20 days with Rule 473) are accurate. Only the optional point is missed, which does not affect the grade.\"}","ttft_ms":4561,"type":"result","duration_ms":9301,"uuid":"1b87df2e-041a-418a-b4f3-4021f47bf332","ttft_stream_ms":1680,"time_to_request_ms":60,"first_content_frame_ms":1681,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
